        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Central &amp; East Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Okinawa</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">1 April to 22 June 1945, after the capture of the Kerama Islands on 26 March; mopping-up ran to 30 June</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The island of Okinawa and the seas and islands around it, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryukyu-islands">Ryukyu Islands</a>, present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Tenth Army under Lieutenant General Simon Bolivar Buckner Jr., with 182,821 personnel at the start, supported by a fleet and by British Task Force 57; the Japanese Thirty-Second Army under Lieutenant General Mitsuru Ushijima, about 100,000 troops at the onset, including drafted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryukyuans">Okinawans</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Americans took the island. The Japanese Thirty-Second Army was destroyed, its commanders died by suicide, and Okinawa became a fleet anchorage and airfield base close to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>.</span></div>
        </div>
